1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,500
Plausible code still needs tests and review. BenchProof is a coding agent for small Python projects,

2
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:18,500
powered by NVIDIA Nemotron on Nebius Token Factory. This walkthrough reviews a saved sample task, not a new live run.

3
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:24,824
Plans, protected imported tests, isolated execution and bounded retries keep its work inspectable.

4
00:00:24,824 --> 00:00:33,000
Here we select the StringCalculator sample. Application files can be approved for editing.

5
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:40,500
Imported tests stay protected from agent changes. Negatives must raise ValueError; empty/positive behavior stays.

6
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:45,810
Only the calculator module is editable.

7
00:00:45,810 --> 00:00:54,500
The saved task includes a model-generated plan. Review its steps and editable files before approval.

8
00:00:54,500 --> 00:01:03,861
Approval binds the recorded plan/source version. Implementation waits for approval; this is completed-task review.

9
00:01:03,861 --> 00:01:13,000
The recorded baseline fails the negative-number check. A real model edit is tested in fresh Docker containers.

10
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Network is denied and resource limits enforced. Candidate and fresh final checks pass: Review Ready.

11
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:27,391
Supplied checks do not prove every requirement. The patch still needs review.

12
00:01:27,391 --> 00:01:35,500
The unified diff shows negative-number validation and the ValueError message.

13
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:43,602
Restore a saved task revision without resetting consumed budgets or changing the local Git repository.

14
00:01:43,602 --> 00:01:53,000
Download the diff, approved plan, checks and event trace. The ZIP is not digitally signed; review before sharing.

15
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:03,278
Try benchproof.vercel.app. The newer release adds skills, harness choices and read-only documentation context.

16
00:02:03,278 --> 00:02:11,000
21 October rehearsal screenshot: pinned skill, single-pass harness and consented documentation reference.

17
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:18,278
Two genuine model calls, one patch, three isolated executions. One public sample, not a held-out benchmark.
